{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDYghG1yfqhuwiiHmepT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WS4KJfzczxz1G6R165RJKx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-batch-hh-5ij5h/7d53973d-c6ec-47f2-bf1b-0f155eb7d218/tool-results/bn5uugv8b.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2433,"cache_read_input_tokens":33369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2433},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d53973d-c6ec-47f2-bf1b-0f155eb7d218","uuid":"081a3eeb-d0ae-4881-aa38-6b2b84b4aea2","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:12:33.304Z","request_id":"req_011CgDYggvRniAdPGF9xAjmB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WS4KJfzczxz1G6R165RJKx":{"file_path":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-batch-hh-5ij5h/7d53973d-c6ec-47f2-bf1b-0f155eb7d218/tool-results/bn5uugv8b.txt"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WS4KJfzczxz1G6R165RJKx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=== README.md\n2\t     1\t# procurement-agent\n3\t     2\t\n4\t     3\tProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\n5\t     4\tinvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\n6\t     5\tpurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\n7\t     6\tvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n8\t     7\t\n9\t     8\t## Architecture\n10\t     9\t\n11\t    10\t```\n12\t    11\tmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\n13\t    12\tstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n14\t    13\t                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n15\t    14\t                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n16\t    15\t                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n17\t    16\t                                   |-- tools:\n18\t    17\t                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n19\t    18\t                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n20\t    19\t                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n21\t    20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n22\t    21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n23\t    22\t```\n24\t    23\t\n25\t    24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n26\t    25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n27\t    26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n28\t    27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n29\t    28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n30\t    29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n31\t    30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n32\t    31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n33\t    32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n34\t    33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n35\t    34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n36\t    35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n37\t    36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n38\t    37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n39\t    38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n40\t    39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n41\t    40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n42\t    41\t\n43\t    42\t## Context size\n44\t    43\t\n45\t    44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n46\t    45\t\n47\t    46\t| method | meaning |\n48\t    47\t|---|---|\n49\t    48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n50\t    49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n51\t    50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n52\t    51\t\n53\t    52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n54\t    53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n55\t    54\t\n56\t    55\t## Operating\n57\t    56\t\n58\t    57\t* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n59\t    58\t  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n60\t    59\t  start while a halt is set.\n61\t    60\t* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n62\t    61\t  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n63\t    62\t  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n64\t    63\t* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n65\t    64\t  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n66\t    65\t\n67\t    66\t## Tests\n68\t    67\t\n69\t    68\t```bash\n70\t    69\tpip install -e '.[test]'\n71\t    70\tpytest -q\n72\t    71\t```\n73\t=== app/ingest.py\n74\t     1\t\"\"\"Inbound documents: vendor quotes and invoices from the mail gateway.\n75\t     2\t\n76\t     3\tThe mail gateway posts each received message to ``/ingest/mail`` signed with\n77\t     4\tan HMAC over the timestamp and body. Accepted documents are stored per\n78\t     5\tbusiness unit and are only ever shown to the model inside an\n79\t     6\t``untrusted_document`` wrapper (tools/documents.py).\n80\t     7\t\"\"\"\n81\t     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n82\t     9\t\n83\t    10\timport base64\n84\t    11\timport email\n85\t    12\timport email.policy\n86\t    13\timport hashlib\n87\t    14\timport hmac\n88\t    15\timport io\n89\t    16\timport re\n90\t    17\timport time\n91\t    18\timport uuid\n92\t    19\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n93\t    20\tfrom pathlib import Path\n94\t    21\t\n95\t    22\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\n96\t    23\tfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n97\t    24\t\n98\t    25\trouter = APIRouter()\n99\t    26\t\n100\t    27\tMAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n101\t    28\tMAX_TEXT_CHARS = 200_000\n102\t    29\tMAX_SKEW_SECONDS = 300\n103\t    30\tALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\", \"message/rfc822\"}\n104\t    31\tSCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\"}\n105\t    32\t\n106\t    33\tINJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n107\t    34\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n108\t    35\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\n109\t    36\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\n110\t    37\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\n111\t    38\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\n112\t    39\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n113\t    40\t]\n114\t    41\t\n115\t    42\t\n116\t    43\tclass Rejected(Exception):\n117\t    44\t    pass\n118\t    45\t\n119\t    46\t\n120\t    47\t@dataclass\n121\t    48\tclass Inbound:\n122\t    49\t    business_unit: str\n123\t    50\t    sender: str\n124\t    51\t    media_type: str\n125\t    52\t    raw: bytes\n126\t    53\t\n127\t    54\t\n128\t    55\tdef verify_signature(key: bytes, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -> None:\n129\t    56\t    try:\n130\t    57\t        ts = int(timestamp)\n131\t    58\t    except ValueError as exc:\n132\t    59\t        raise Rejected(\"bad timestamp\") from exc\n133\t    60\t    if abs(time.time() - ts) > MAX_SKEW_SECONDS:\n134\t    61\t        raise Rejected(\"stale request\")\n135\t    62\t    expected = hmac.new(key, f\"{timestamp}.\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n136\t    63\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature):\n137\t    64\t        raise Rejected(\"bad signature\")\n138\t    65\t\n139\t    66\t\n140\t    67\tdef extract_text(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n141\t    68\t    if doc.media_type == \"application/pdf\":\n142\t    69\t        reader = PdfReader(io.BytesIO(doc.raw))\n143\t    70\t        if len(reader.pages) > 50:\n144\t    71\t            raise Rejected(\"too many pages\")\n145\t    72\t        return \"\\n\".join(page.extract_text() or \"\" for page in reader.pages)\n146\t    73\t    if doc.media_type == \"message/rfc822\":\n147\t    74\t        msg = email.message_from_bytes(doc.raw, policy=email.policy.default)\n148\t    75\t        body = msg.get_body(preferencelist=(\"plain\", \"html\"))\n149\t    76\t        return body.get_content() if body is not None else \"\"\n150\t    77\t    return doc.raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n151\t    78\t\n152\t    79\t\n153\t    80\tdef scan_for_injection(text: str) -> list[str]:\n154\t    81\t    return [p.pattern for p in INJECTION_PATTERNS if p.search(text)]\n155\t    82\t\n156\t    83\t\n157\t    84\tdef validate(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n158\t    85\t    if doc.media_type not in ALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n159\t    86\t        raise Rejected(f\"media type {doc.media_type} not accepted\")\n160\t    87\t    if len(doc.raw) > MAX_BODY_BYTES:\n161\t    88\t        raise Rejected(\"document too large\")\n162\t    89\t    try:\n163\t    90\t        text = extract_text(doc)\n164\t    91\t    except Rejected:\n165\t    92\t        raise\n166\t    93\t    except Exception as exc:\n167\t    94\t        raise Rejected(f\"unreadable document: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n168\t    95\t    if len(text) > MAX_TEXT_CHARS:\n169\t    96\t        raise Rejected(\"extracted text too long\")\n170\t    97\t    if doc.media_type in SCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n171\t    98\t        findings = scan_for_injection(text)\n172\t    99\t        if findings:\n173\t   100\t            raise Rejected(\"possible prompt injection: \" + \"; \".join(findings))\n174\t   101\t    return text\n175\t   102\t\n176\t   103\t\n177\t   104\t@router.post(\"/ingest/mail\")\n178\t   105\tasync def ingest_mail(request: Request) -> dict:\n179\t   106\t    body = await request.body()\n180\t   107\t    if len(body) > MAX_BODY_BYTES * 2:\n181\t   108\t        raise HTTPException(413, \"payload too large\")\n182\t   109\t    key = Path(request.app.state.settings.mail_gateway_hmac_path).read_bytes().strip()\n183\t   110\t    try:\n184\t   111\t        verify_signature(\n185\t   112\t            key,\n186\t   113\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Timestamp\", \"\"),\n187\t   114\t            body,\n188\t   115\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Signature\", \"\"),\n189\t   116\t        )\n190\t   117\t    except Rejected as exc:\n191\t   118\t        raise HTTPException(401, str(exc)) from exc\n192\t   119\t\n193\t   120\t    payload = await request.json()\n194\t   121\t    doc = Inbound(\n195\t   122\t        business_unit=payload[\"business_unit\"],\n196\t   123\t        sender=payload[\"from\"],\n197\t   124\t        media_type=payload[\"media_type\"],\n198\t   125\t        raw=base64.b64decode(payload[\"content_b64\"], validate=True),\n199\t   126\t    )\n200\t   127\t    doc_id = f\"doc-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:20]}\"\n201\t   128\t    pool = request.app.state.pool\n202\t   129\t    try:\n203\t   130\t        text = validate(doc)\n204\t   131\t    except Rejected as exc:\n205\t   132\t        await pool.execute(\n206\t   133\t            \"\"\"\n207\t   134\t            INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, reject_reason, received_at)\n208\t   135\t            VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'quarantined', $6, now())\n209\t   136\t            \"\"\",\n210\t   137\t            doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n211\t   138\t            hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), str(exc)[:500],\n212\t   139\t        )\n213\t   140\t        return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"quarantined\"}\n214\t   141\t\n215\t   142\t    await pool.execute(\n216\t   143\t        \"\"\"\n217\t   144\t        INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, text, received_at)\n218\t   145\t        VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'accepted', $6, now())\n219\t   146\t        \"\"\",\n220\t   147\t        doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n221\t   148\t        hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), text,\n222\t   149\t    )\n223\t   150\t    return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"accepted\"}\n224\t=== app/tools/memory.py\n225\t     1\t\"\"\"Per-department notes kept between runs (Postgres ``dept_notes``).\n226\t     2\t\n227\t     3\tWrites are restricted to a fixed set of note kinds, length-limited, checked\n228\t     4\tfor instruction-like content, and stored as unverified with a 30-day expiry\n229\t     5\tuntil a procurement lead verifies them in the admin UI. Every row records\n230\t     6\twho wrote it, from which run and source document, and the context size at\n231\t     7\tthe time.\n232\t     8\t\"\"\"\n233\t     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n234\t    10\t\n235\t    11\timport re\n236\t    12\timport uuid\n237\t    13\tfrom typing import Any\n238\t    14\t\n239\t    15\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n240\t    16\tfrom app.tools import Tool\n241\t    17\t\n242\t    18\tNOTE_KINDS = (\"vendor_preference\", \"contract_term\", \"budget_note\", \"contact\")\n243\t    19\tMAX_NOTE_CHARS = 800\n244\t    20\tINSTRUCTION_LIKE = [\n245\t    21\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(ignore|disregard|override)\\b.{0,40}\\b(instruction|policy|approval|rule)s?\\b\"),\n246\t    22\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(always|never|must)\\b.{0,40}\\b(approve|pay|skip|send|transfer)\\b\"),\n247\t    23\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are|assistant:)\\b\"),\n248\t    24\t    re.compile(r\"https?://\"),\n249\t    25\t]\n250\t    26\t\n251\t    27\t\n252\t    28\tclass NoteRejected(Exception):\n253\t    29\t    pass\n254\t    30\t\n255\t    31\t\n256\t    32\tdef check_note(text: str) -> None:\n257\t    33\t    if len(text) > MAX_NOTE_CHARS:\n258\t    34\t        raise NoteRejected(\"note too long\")\n259\t    35\t    for pattern in INSTRUCTION_LIKE:\n260\t    36\t        if pattern.search(text):\n261\t    37\t            raise NoteRejected(\"note looks like an instruction\")\n262\t    38\t\n263\t    39\t\n264\t    40\tdef tools(deps) -> list[Tool]:\n265\t    41\t    pool = deps.pool\n266\t    42\t\n267\t    43\t    async def memory_read(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n268\t    44\t        business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant\n269\t    45\t        rows = await pool.fetch(\n270\t    46\t            \"\"\"\n271\t    47\t            SELECT note_id, kind, body, verified, writer_instance, created_at\n272\t    48\t            FROM dept_notes\n273\t    49\t            WHERE business_unit = $1\n274\t    50\t              AND department = $2\n275\t    51\t              AND NOT quarantined\n276\t    52\t              AND (verified OR expires_at > now())\n277\t    53\t            ORDER BY created_at DESC\n278\t    54\t            LIMIT 20\n279\t    55\t            \"\"\",\n280\t    56\t            business_unit,\n281\t    57\t            args[\"department\"],\n282\t    58\t        )\n283\t    59\t        return [\n284\t    60\t            {\n285\t    61\t                \"note_id\": r[\"note_id\"],\n286\t    62\t                \"kind\": r[\"kind\"],\n287\t    63\t                \"body\": r[\"body\"],\n288\t    64\t                \"trust\": \"verified\" if r[\"verified\"] else \"unverified\",\n289\t    65\t                \"written\": r[\"created_at\"].isoformat(),\n290\t    66\t            }\n291\t    67\t            for r in rows\n292\t    68\t        ]\n293\t    69\t\n294\t    70\t    async def memory_write(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n295\t    71\t        if args[\"kind\"] not in NOTE_KINDS:\n296\t    72\t            raise NoteRejected(f\"unknown note kind {args['kind']}\")\n297\t    73\t        check_note(args[\"body\"])\n298\t    74\t        note_id = f\"note-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n299\t    75\t        ctx = deps.current_context(ident)\n300\t    76\t        await pool.execute(\n301\t    77\t            \"\"\"\n302\t    78\t            INSERT INTO dept_notes (\n303\t    79\t                note_id, business_unit, department, kind, body,\n304\t    80\t                verified, quarantined, expires_at,\n305\t    81\t                writer_instance, writer_type_id, run_id, source_doc_id,\n306\t    82\t                delegated_subject, context_tokens, context_method, created_at\n307\t    83\t            ) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, false, false, now() + interval '30 days',\n308\t    84\t                      $6, $7, $8, $9, $10, $11, $12, now())\n309\t    85\t            \"\"\",\n310\t    86\t            note_id,\n311\t    87\t            ident.tenant,\n312\t    88\t            args[\"department\"],\n313\t    89\t            args[\"kind\"],\n314\t    90\t            args[\"body\"],\n315\t    91\t            ident.agent_instance_id,\n316\t    92\t            ident.agent_type_id,\n317\t    93\t            ident.run_id,\n318\t    94\t            args.get(\"source_doc_id\"),\n319\t    95\t            ident.delegated_subject,\n320\t    96\t            ctx.tokens,\n321\t    97\t            ctx.method,\n322\t    98\t        )\n323\t    99\t        return {\"note_id\": note_id, \"status\": \"stored_unverified\"}\n324\t   100\t\n325\t   101\t    return [\n326\t   102\t        Tool(\n327\t   103\t            name=\"memory_read\",\n328\t   104\t            description=(\n329\t   105\t                \"Read saved notes for a department. business_unit defaults to the current one; \"\n330\t   106\t                \"shared-services staff may look up another unit's notes.\"\n331\t   107\t            ),\n332\t   108\t            input_schema={\n333\t   109\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n334\t   110\t                \"properties\": {\n335\t   111\t                    \"department\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n336\t   112\t                    \"business_unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 32},\n337\t   113\t                },\n338\t   114\t                \"required\": [\"department\"],\n339\t   115\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n340\t   116\t            },\n341\t   117\t            invoke=memory_read,\n342\t   118\t        ),\n343\t   119\t        Tool(\n344\t   120\t            name=\"memory_write\",\n345\t   121\t            description=\"Save a short factual note for a department (vendor preference, contract term, budget note, contact).\",\n346\t   122\t            input_schema={\n347\t   123\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n348\t   124\t                \"properties\": {\n349\t   125\t                    \"department\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n350\t   126\t                    \"kind\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": list(NOTE_KINDS)},\n351\t   127\t                    \"body\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": MAX_NOTE_CHARS},\n352\t   128\t                    \"source_doc_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n353\t   129\t                },\n354\t   130\t                \"required\": [\"department\", \"kind\", \"body\"],\n355\t   131\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n356\t   132\t            },\n357\t   133\t            invoke=memory_write,\n358\t   134\t        ),\n359\t   135\t    ]\n360\t=== app/tools/documents.py\n361\t     1\t\"\"\"Document tools: read an ingested quote or invoice, and extract line items.\"\"\"\n362\t     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n363\t     3\t\n364\t     4\tfrom typing import Any\n365\t     5\t\n366\t     6\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n367\t     7\tfrom app.tools import Tool\n368\t     8\t\n369\t     9\tUNTRUSTED_WRAPPER = (\n370\t    10\t    \"<untrusted_document source={source!r} doc_id={doc_id!r} media_type={media_type!r}>\\n\"\n371\t    11\t    \"{text}\\n\"\n372\t    12\t    \"</untrusted_document>\"\n373\t    13\t)\n374\t    14\t\n375\t    15\t\n376\t    16\tdef tools(deps) -> list[Tool]:\n377\t    17\t    pool = deps.pool\n378\t    18\t\n379\t    19\t    async def read_document(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> str:\n380\t    20\t        row = await pool.fetchrow(\n381\t    21\t            \"\"\"\n382\t    22\t            SELECT doc_id, source, media_type, text\n383\t    23\t            FROM documents\n384\t    24\t            WHERE doc_id = $1 AND business_unit = $2 AND status = 'accepted'\n385\t    25\t            \"\"\",\n386\t    26\t            args[\"doc_id\"],\n387\t    27\t            ident.tenant,\n388\t    28\t        )\n389\t    29\t        if row is None:\n390\t    30\t            return \"document not found\"\n391\t    31\t        return UNTRUSTED_WRAPPER.format(\n392\t    32\t            source=row[\"source\"], doc_id=row[\"doc_id\"], media_type=row[\"media_type\"], text=row[\"text\"]\n393\t    33\t        )\n394\t    34\t\n395\t    35\t    async def extract_line_items(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n396\t    36\t        return await deps.extractor.extract(ident, args[\"doc_id\"], deps.current_budget(ident))\n397\t    37\t\n398\t    38\t    return [\n399\t    39\t        Tool(\n400\t    40\t            name=\"read_document\",\n401\t    41\t            description=\"Read the text of an ingested vendor quote, invoice, or email by doc_id.\",\n402\t    42\t            input_schema={\n403\t    43\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n404\t    44\t                \"properties\": {\"doc_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64}},\n405\t    45\t                \"required\": [\"doc_id\"],\n406\t    46\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n407\t    47\t            },\n408\t    48\t            invoke=read_document,\n409\t    49\t        ),\n410\t    50\t        Tool(\n411\t    51\t            name=\"extract_line_items\",\n412\t    52\t            description=\"Extract structured line items (sku, description, qty, unit price, currency) from a document.\",\n413\t    53\t            input_schema={\n414\t    54\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n415\t    55\t                \"properties\": {\"doc_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64}},\n416\t    56\t                \"required\": [\"doc_id\"],\n417\t    57\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n418\t    58\t            },\n419\t    59\t            invoke=extract_line_items,\n420\t    60\t        ),\n421\t    61\t    ]\n422\t=== app/tools/__init__.py\n423\t     1\t\"\"\"Tool registry.\n424\t     2\t\n425\t     3\tEach agent role gets the tools listed for it in config/tools.yaml. The model\n426\t     4\tonly sees schemas for those tools, and the loop rejects any call to a name\n427\t     5\tthat is not in the run's registry.\n428\t     6\t\"\"\"\n429\t     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n430\t     8\t\n431\t     9\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n432\t    10\tfrom functools import lru_cache\n433\t    11\tfrom typing import Any, Awaitable, Callable\n434\t    12\t\n435\t    13\timport yaml\n436\t    14\t\n437\t    15\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n438\t    16\t\n439\t    17\tDEFAULT_ROLE = \"procurement\"\n440\t    18\t\n441\t    19\tInvoke = Callable[[dict[str, Any], RunIdentity], Awaitable[Any]]\n442\t    20\t\n443\t    21\t\n444\t    22\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n445\t    23\tclass Tool:\n446\t    24\t    name: str\n447\t    25\t    description: str\n448\t    26\t    input_schema: dict[str, Any]\n449\t    27\t    invoke: Invoke\n450\t    28\t    target_field: str | None = None\n451\t    29\t\n452\t    30\t    def target_of(self, args: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n453\t    31\t        if self.target_field is None:\n454\t    32\t            return self.name\n455\t    33\t        return str(args.get(self.target_field, \"\"))\n456\t    34\t\n457\t    35\t    def schema(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n458\t    36\t        return {\"name\": self.name, \"description\": self.description, \"input_schema\": self.input_schema}\n459\t    37\t\n460\t    38\t\n461\t    39\tclass ToolRegistry:\n462\t    40\t    def __init__(self, tools: list[Tool]):\n463\t    41\t        self._tools = {t.name: t for t in tools}\n464\t    42\t\n465\t    43\t    def get(self, name: str) -> Tool | None:\n466\t    44\t        return self._tools.get(name)\n467\t    45\t\n468\t    46\t    def names(self) -> list[str]:\n469\t    47\t        return sorted(self._tools)\n470\t    48\t\n471\t    49\t    def schemas(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n472\t    50\t        return [self._tools[n].schema() for n in self.names()]\n473\t    51\t\n474\t    52\t\n475\t    53\t@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n476\t    54\tdef _role_tools(path: str) -> dict[str, list[str]]:\n477\t    55\t    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n478\t    56\t        cfg = yaml.safe_load(fh)\n479\t    57\t    return {role: list(spec[\"tools\"].keys()) for role, spec in cfg[\"roles\"].items()}\n480\t    58\t\n481\t    59\t\n482\t    60\tdef build_registry(role: str, ident: RunIdentity, deps) -> ToolRegistry:\n483\t    61\t    from app.tools import documents, erp, memory, payments, slack\n484\t    62\t\n485\t    63\t    available: dict[str, Tool] = {}\n486\t    64\t    for module in (documents, erp, memory, payments, slack):\n487\t    65\t        for tool in module.tools(deps):\n488\t    66\t            available[tool.name] = tool\n489\t    67\t\n490\t    68\t    roles = _role_tools(str(deps.settings.tools_path))\n491\t    69\t    allowed = roles.get(role, roles[DEFAULT_ROLE])\n492\t    70\t    return ToolRegistry([available[name] for name in allowed if name in available])\n493\t=== app/context_size.py\n494\t     1\t\"\"\"Decision-time context size.\n495\t     2\t\n496\t     3\tCounting method (documented in README, \"Context size\"):\n497\t     4\t\n498\t     5\t1. Before each model call, the exact request (system prompt, messages and\n499\t     6\t   tool schemas) is sent to the provider's token-counting endpoint. The\n500\t     7\t   returned ``input_tokens`` is recorded with method ``count_tokens_api``.\n501\t     8\t   This is the size of the context the model decides on, including any\n502\t     9\t   prefix that will be served from the prompt cache.\n503\t    10\t2. If counting fails, the value is taken after the call from the response\n504\t    11\t   usage as ``input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens +\n505\t    12\t   cache_creation_input_tokens`` and recorded with method\n506\t    13\t   ``usage_sum_estimate``.\n507\t    14\t3. If neither is available the value is ``NULL`` with method\n508\t    15\t   ``unavailable``. It is never recorded as zero.\n509\t    16\t\n510\t    17\t``compacted`` is true when the harness dropped or summarized earlier turns\n511\t    18\tbefore this call. Provider-side truncation is not visible to the harness and\n512\t    19\tis listed as a known limit.\n513\t    20\t\"\"\"\n514\t    21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n515\t    22\t\n516\t    23\timport logging\n517\t    24\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n518\t    25\t\n519\t    26\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n520\t    27\t\n521\t    28\t\n522\t    29\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n523\t    30\tclass ContextMeasure:\n524\t    31\t    tokens: int | None\n525\t    32\t    method: str\n526\t    33\t    compacted: bool\n527\t    34\t\n528\t    35\t    @classmethod\n529\t    36\t    def unavailable(cls, compacted: bool = False) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n530\t    37\t        return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\n531\t    38\t\n532\t    39\t    def finalize(self, usage) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n533\t    40\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n534\t    41\t            return self\n535\t    42\t        if usage is None:\n536\t    43\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n537\t    44\t        total = (\n538\t    45\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n539\t    46\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n540\t    47\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n541\t    48\t        )\n542\t    49\t        if total <= 0:\n543\t    50\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n544\t    51\t        return replace(self, tokens=total, method=\"usage_sum_estimate\")\n545\t    52\t\n546\t    53\t    def otel_attributes(self) -> dict:\n547\t    54\t        attrs = {\n548\t    55\t            \"procurement.context.method\": self.method,\n549\t    56\t            \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": self.compacted,\n550\t    57\t        }\n551\t    58\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n552\t    59\t            attrs[\"procurement.context.tokens\"] = self.tokens\n553\t    60\t        return attrs\n554\t    61\t\n555\t    62\t\n556\t    63\tasync def measure_context(client, request: dict, compacted: bool) -> ContextMeasure:\n557\t    64\t    try:\n558\t    65\t        counted = await client.messages.count_tokens(\n559\t    66\t            model=request[\"model\"],\n560\t    67\t            system=request[\"system\"],\n561\t    68\t            messages=request[\"messages\"],\n562\t    69\t            tools=request[\"tools\"],\n563\t    70\t        )\n564\t    71\t        return ContextMeasure(int(counted.input_tokens), \"count_tokens_api\", compacted)\n565\t    72\t    except Exception:  # counting is best effort; finalize() falls back to usage\n566\t    73\t        log.warning(\"token count failed; falling back to usage\", exc_info=True)\n567\t    74\t        return ContextMeasure(tokens=None, method=\"pending_usage\", compacted=compacted)\n568\t=== app/audit.py\n569\t     1\t\"\"\"Execution audit graph.\n570\t     2\t\n571\t     3\tEvery step of a run is one row in ``audit_events``. Rows link to their parent\n572\t     4\tstep, so a run can be rebuilt as a tree: run -> model decision -> proposed\n573\t     5\ttool call -> authorization decision -> result or error. Writes are\n574\t     6\tsynchronous and are made before the action they describe; if the write\n575\t     7\tfails, the caller raises and the action does not run.\n576\t     8\t\"\"\"\n577\t     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n578\t    10\t\n579\t    11\timport hashlib\n580\t    12\timport json\n581\t    13\timport uuid\n582\t    14\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n583\t    15\tfrom typing import Any\n584\t    16\t\n585\t    17\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n586\t    18\t\n587\t    19\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure\n588\t    20\tfrom app.identity import IDENTITY_FIELDS, RunIdentity\n589\t    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_value\n590\t    22\t\n591\t    23\tEVENT_KINDS = {\n592\t    24\t    \"run_started\",\n593\t    25\t    \"run_finished\",\n594\t    26\t    \"run_halted\",\n595\t    27\t    \"model_decision\",\n596\t    28\t    \"tool_proposed\",\n597\t    29\t    \"authz_decision\",\n598\t    30\t    \"approval_requested\",\n599\t    31\t    \"approval_decided\",\n600\t    32\t    \"tool_result\",\n601\t    33\t    \"tool_error\",\n602\t    34\t    \"tool_denied\",\n603\t    35\t    \"budget_exceeded\",\n604\t    36\t    \"subagent_started\",\n605\t    37\t    \"subagent_finished\",\n606\t    38\t    \"background_job\",\n607\t    39\t}\n608\t    40\t\n609\t    41\t_INSERT = \"\"\"\n610\t    42\tINSERT INTO audit_events (\n611\t    43\t    node_id, parent_node_id, run_id, ts, kind,\n612\t    44\t    accountable_party, operational_owner, tenant,\n613\t    45\t    agent_type_id, agent_instance_id, trace_id, span_id,\n614\t    46\t    delegated_subject, agent_principal, parent_instance_id,\n615\t    47\t    policy_version, approval_id, operation_id,\n616\t    48\t    context_tokens, context_method, context_compacted,\n617\t    49\t    payload\n618\t    50\t) VALUES (\n619\t    51\t    $1, $2, $3, $4, $5,\n620\t    52\t    $6, $7, $8,\n621\t    53\t    $9, $10, $11, $12,\n622\t    54\t    $13, $14, $15,\n623\t    55\t    $16, $17, $18,\n624\t    56\t    $19, $20, $21,\n625\t    57\t    $22::jsonb\n626\t    58\t)\n627\t    59\t\"\"\"\n628\t    60\t\n629\t    61\t\n630\t    62\tdef summarize_args(args: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n631\t    63\t    \"\"\"Key arguments for the record, with secrets and account numbers redacted.\"\"\"\n632\t    64\t    return {k: redact_value(v) for k, v in args.items()}\n633\t    65\t\n634\t    66\t\n635\t    67\tdef digest(value: Any) -> str:\n636\t    68\t    raw = json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n637\t    69\t    return hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n638\t    70\t\n639\t    71\t\n640\t    72\tasync def record(\n641\t    73\t    pool,\n642\t    74\t    ident: RunIdentity,\n643\t    75\t    *,\n644\t    76\t    kind: str,\n645\t    77\t    payload: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n646\t    78\t    parent: str | None = None,\n647\t    79\t    context: ContextMeasure | None = None,\n648\t    80\t    policy_version: str | None = None,\n649\t    81\t    approval_id: str | None = None,\n650\t    82\t    operation_id: str | None = None,\n651\t    83\t) -> str:\n652\t    84\t    if kind not in EVENT_KINDS:\n653\t    85\t        raise ValueError(f\"unknown audit kind {kind}\")\n654\t    86\t    for name in IDENTITY_FIELDS:\n655\t    87\t        if not getattr(ident, name):\n656\t    88\t            raise ValueError(f\"audit record missing {name}\")\n657\t    89\t    span_ctx = trace.get_current_span().get_span_context()\n658\t    90\t    span_id = format(span_ctx.span_id, \"016x\") if span_ctx.is_valid else None\n659\t    91\t    node_id = f\"node-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n660\t    92\t    measure = context or ContextMeasure.unavailable()\n661\t    93\t    await pool.execute(\n662\t    94\t        _INSERT,\n663\t    95\t        node_id,\n664\t    96\t        parent,\n665\t    97\t        ident.run_id,\n666\t    98\t        datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n667\t    99\t        kind,\n668\t   100\t        ident.accountable_party,\n669\t   101\t        ident.operational_owner,\n670\t   102\t        ident.tenant,\n671\t   103\t        ident.agent_type_id,\n672\t   104\t        ident.agent_instance_id,\n673\t   105\t        ident.trace_id,\n674\t   106\t        span_id,\n675\t   107\t        ident.delegated_subject,\n676\t   108\t        ident.agent_principal,\n677\t   109\t        ident.parent_instance_id,\n678\t   110\t        policy_version,\n679\t   111\t        approval_id,\n680\t   112\t        operation_id,\n681\t   113\t        measure.tokens,\n682\t   114\t        measure.method,\n683\t   115\t        measure.compacted,\n684\t   116\t        json.dumps(redact_value(payload or {}), default=str),\n685\t   117\t    )\n686\t   118\t    return node_id\n687\t=== app/loop.py\n688\t     1\t\"\"\"Procurement agent run loop.\n689\t     2\t\n690\t     3\tGraph: model turn -> (tool calls -> gate -> integration)* -> model turn ...\n691\t     4\tEvery edge writes an audit node before the next step runs. Budgets are\n692\t     5\tchecked before each model turn and each tool call.\n693\t     6\t\"\"\"\n694\t     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n695\t     8\t\n696\t     9\timport hashlib\n697\t    10\timport logging\n698\t    11\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n699\t    12\tfrom typing import Any\n700\t    13\t\n701\t    14\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n702\t    15\t\n703\t    16\tfrom app import audit, killswitch\n704\t    17\tfrom app.budget import Budget, BudgetExceeded\n705\t    18\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure, measure_context\n706\t    19\tfrom app.gate import PolicyGate\n707\t    20\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n708\t    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n709\t    22\tfrom app.tools import ToolRegistry, build_registry\n710\t    23\t\n711\t    24\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n712\t    25\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.loop\")\n713\t    26\t\n714\t    27\tCOMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES = 40\n715\t    28\tKEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES = 12\n716\t    29\t\n717\t    30\t\n718\t    31\t@dataclass\n719\t    32\tclass AgentDeps:\n720\t    33\t    settings: Any\n721\t    34\t    pool: Any\n722\t    35\t    gate: PolicyGate\n723\t    36\t    erp: Any\n724\t    37\t    slack: Any\n725\t    38\t    broker: Any\n726\t    39\t    extractor: Any = None\n727\t    40\t    _budgets: dict[str, Budget] = field(default_factory=dict)\n728\t    41\t    _contexts: dict[str, ContextMeasure] = field(default_factory=dict)\n729\t    42\t\n730\t    43\t    def current_budget(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> Budget:\n731\t    44\t        return self._budgets[ident.run_id]\n732\t    45\t\n733\t    46\t    def current_context(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> ContextMeasure:\n734\t    47\t        return self._contexts.get(ident.agent_instance_id, ContextMeasure.unavailable())\n735\t    48\t\n736\t    49\t    def erp_scope_for(self, operation: str) -> str:\n737\t    50\t        scopes = self.settings.policy[\"erp\"][\"operation_scopes\"]\n738\t    51\t        return scopes.get(operation, \"erp.read\")\n739\t    52\t\n740\t    53\t    async def execute_tool(self, ident, registry: ToolRegistry, use, parent: str, ctx: ContextMeasure) -> dict:\n741\t    54\t        self._contexts[ident.agent_instance_id] = ctx\n742\t    55\t        proposed = await audit.record(\n743\t    56\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_proposed\", parent=parent, context=ctx,\n744\t    57\t            payload={\"tool\": use.name, \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"args\": audit.summarize_args(use.input)},\n745\t    58\t        )\n746\t    59\t        tool = registry.get(use.name)\n747\t    60\t        if tool is None:\n748\t    61\t            await audit.record(\n749\t    62\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_denied\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n750\t    63\t                policy_version=self.gate.version, payload={\"reason\": \"tool not in role allowlist\"},\n751\t    64\t            )\n752\t    65\t            return _error(use.id, f\"tool {use.name} is not available to this agent\")\n753\t    66\t\n754\t    67\t        decision = await self.gate.authorize(ident, tool, use.input)\n755\t    68\t        authz = await audit.record(\n756\t    69\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"authz_decision\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n757\t    70\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n758\t    71\t            payload={\"allow\": decision.allow, \"reason\": decision.reason, \"pending\": decision.pending},\n759\t    72\t        )\n760\t    73\t        if not decision.allow:\n761\t    74\t            if decision.pending:\n762\t    75\t                return _error(use.id, f\"approval requested ({decision.approval_id}); do not retry until approved\")\n763\t    76\t            return _error(use.id, f\"denied: {decision.reason}\")\n764\t    77\t\n765\t    78\t        operation_id = f\"op-{hashlib.sha256((authz + use.id).encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}\"\n766\t    79\t        try:\n767\t    80\t            with tracer.start_as_current_span(f\"execute_tool {use.name}\") as span:\n768\t    81\t                for k, v in ctx.otel_attributes().items():\n769\t    82\t                    span.set_attribute(k, v)\n770\t    83\t                output = await tool.invoke(use.input, ident)\n771\t    84\t        except BudgetExceeded:\n772\t    85\t            raise\n773\t    86\t        except Exception as exc:\n774\t    87\t            await audit.record(\n775\t    88\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_error\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n776\t    89\t                policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n777\t    90\t                operation_id=operation_id,\n778\t    91\t                payload={\"error_type\": type(exc).__name__, \"error\": str(exc)[:500]},\n779\t    92\t            )\n780\t    93\t            return _error(use.id, f\"{use.name} failed: {type(exc).__name__}\")\n781\t    94\t\n782\t    95\t        await audit.record(\n783\t    96\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_result\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n784\t    97\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n785\t    98\t            operation_id=operation_id,\n786\t    99\t            payload={\"result_sha256\": audit.digest(output), \"result\": output},\n787\t   100\t        )\n788\t   101\t        return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"content\": redact_for_model(output)}\n789\t   102\t\n790\t   103\t\n791\t   104\tdef _error(tool_use_id: str, message: str) -> dict:\n792\t   105\t    return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": tool_use_id, \"is_error\": True, \"content\": message}\n793\t   106\t\n794\t   107\t\n795\t   108\tdef _compact(messages: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], bool]:\n796\t   109\t    if len(messages) <= COMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES:\n797\t   110\t        return messages, False\n798\t   111\t    head, tail = messages[:1], messages[-KEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES:]\n799\t   112\t    while tail and tail[0][\"role\"] != \"assistant\":\n800\t   113\t        tail = tail[1:]\n801\t   114\t    note = {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[earlier tool exchanges were removed to save space]\"}\n802\t   115\t    return head + [note] + tail, True\n803\t   116\t\n804\t   117\t\n805\t   118\tclass ProcurementAgent:\n806\t   119\t    def __init__(self, *, client, deps: AgentDeps, system_prompt: str, role: str = \"procurement\"):\n807\t   120\t        self.client = client\n808\t   121\t        self.deps = deps\n809\t   122\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n810\t   123\t        self.role = role\n811\t   124\t\n812\t   125\t    async def run(self, ident: RunIdentity, task: str) -> str | None:\n813\t   126\t        pool = self.deps.pool\n814\t   127\t        await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n815\t   128\t        budget = Budget.for_run(self.deps.settings.budgets, ident)\n816\t   129\t        await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n817\t   130\t        self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n818\t   131\t        registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n819\t   132\t\n820\t   133\t        run_node = await audit.record(\n821\t   134\t            pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n822\t   135\t            payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n823\t   136\t        )\n824\t   137\t        messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n825\t   138\t        try:\n826\t   139\t            while True:\n827\t   140\t                budget.check_step()\n828\t   141\t                messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\n829\t   142\t                request = {\n830\t   143\t                    \"model\": self.deps.settings.model_id,\n831\t   144\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n832\t   145\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n833\t   146\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n834\t   147\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n835\t   148\t                }\n836\t   149\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted)\n837\t   150\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n838\t   151\t                budget.charge_model(self.deps.settings.model_id, response.usage)\n839\t   152\t                await budget.flush(pool)\n840\t   153\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n841\t   154\t                decision = await audit.record(\n842\t   155\t                    pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n843\t   156\t                    payload={\n844\t   157\t                        \"requested_model\": request[\"model\"],\n845\t   158\t                        \"served_model\": response.model,\n846\t   159\t                        \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason,\n847\t   160\t                        \"proposed_tools\": [b.name for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"],\n848\t   161\t                    },\n849\t   162\t                )\n850\t   163\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n851\t   164\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n852\t   165\t                if not uses:\n853\t   166\t                    final = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n854\t   167\t                    await audit.record(pool, ident, kind=\"run_finished\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n855\t   168\t                                       payload={\"final_sha256\": audit.digest(final)})\n856\t   169\t                    return final\n857\t   170\t                results = []\n858\t   171\t                for use in uses:\n859\t   172\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n860\t   173\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n861\t   174\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n862\t   175\t        except BudgetExceeded as exc:\n863\t   176\t            await audit.record(\n864\t   177\t                pool, ident, kind=\"budget_exceeded\", parent=run_node,\n865\t   178\t                payload={\"limit\": exc.limit, \"used\": str(exc.used), \"allowed\": str(exc.allowed)},\n866\t   179\t            )\n867\t   180\t            await self.deps.slack.post(\n868\t   181\t                channel=\"#procurement-agent-ops\",\n869\t   182\t                text=f\"Run {ident.run_id} ({ident.tenant}) stopped: {exc.limit} exceeded.\",\n870\t   183\t            )\n871\t   184\t            return None\n872\t   185\t        finally:\n873\t   186\t            self.deps._budgets.pop(ident.run_id, None)\n874\t=== app/extractor.py\n875\t     1\t\"\"\"Line-item extraction sub-agent.\n876\t     2\t\n877\t     3\tThe parent procurement agent delegates structured extraction to a smaller\n878\t     4\tmodel. The child runs under its own instance id, links to its parent in the\n879\t     5\taudit graph, charges the parent's budget, and gets the extractor tool role.\n880\t     6\t\"\"\"\n881\t     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n882\t     8\t\n883\t     9\timport json\n884\t    10\timport logging\n885\t    11\tfrom typing import Any\n886\t    12\t\n887\t    13\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n888\t    14\t\n889\t    15\tfrom app import audit\n890\t    16\tfrom app.budget import Budget\n891\t    17\tfrom app.context_size import measure_context\n892\t    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n893\t    19\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n894\t    20\tfrom app.tools import build_registry\n895\t    21\t\n896\t    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n897\t    23\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.extractor\")\n898\t    24\t\n899\t    25\tEXTRACTOR_ROLE = \"line_item_extractor\"\n900\t    26\tMAX_TURNS = 4\n901\t    27\t\n902\t    28\tLINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS = {\"sku\", \"description\", \"quantity\", \"unit_price_cents\", \"currency\"}\n903\t    29\t\n904\t    30\t\n905\t    31\tclass ExtractionFailed(Exception):\n906\t    32\t    pass\n907\t    33\t\n908\t    34\t\n909\t    35\tclass LineItemExtractor:\n910\t    36\t    def __init__(self, *, client, settings, deps, system_prompt: str):\n911\t    37\t        self.client = client\n912\t    38\t        self.settings = settings\n913\t    39\t        self.deps = deps\n914\t    40\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n915\t    41\t\n916\t    42\t    async def extract(self, parent: RunIdentity, doc_id: str, budget: Budget) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n917\t    43\t        budget.check_subagent()\n918\t    44\t        ident = parent.child(role=EXTRACTOR_ROLE)\n919\t    45\t        registry = build_registry(EXTRACTOR_ROLE, ident, self.deps)\n920\t    46\t        task = f\"Extract every line item from document {doc_id}. Return JSON only.\"\n921\t    47\t\n922\t    48\t        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"gen_ai.invoke_agent line_item_extractor\") as span:\n923\t    49\t            span.set_attribute(\"gen_ai.agent.id\", ident.agent_instance_id)\n924\t    50\t            span.set_attribute(\"procurement.parent_instance_id\", parent.agent_instance_id)\n925\t    51\t            start_node = await audit.record(\n926\t    52\t                self.deps.pool,\n927\t    53\t                ident,\n928\t    54\t                kind=\"subagent_started\",\n929\t    55\t                payload={\n930\t    56\t                    \"role\": EXTRACTOR_ROLE,\n931\t    57\t                    \"doc_id\": doc_id,\n932\t    58\t                    \"parent_prompt_ref\": format(span.get_span_context().span_id, \"016x\"),\n933\t    59\t                    \"tools\": registry.names(),\n934\t    60\t                },\n935\t    61\t            )\n936\t    62\t\n937\t    63\t            messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n938\t    64\t            for _turn in range(MAX_TURNS):\n939\t    65\t                budget.check_step()\n940\t    66\t                request = {\n941\t    67\t                    \"model\": self.settings.extractor_model_id,\n942\t    68\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n943\t    69\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n944\t    70\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n945\t    71\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n946\t    72\t                }\n947\t    73\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted=False)\n948\t    74\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n949\t    75\t                budget.charge_model(self.settings.extractor_model_id, response.usage)\n950\t    76\t                await budget.flush(self.deps.pool)\n951\t    77\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n952\t    78\t                decision = await audit.record(\n953\t    79\t                    self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,\n954\t    80\t                    payload={\"requested_model\": request[\"model\"], \"served_model\": response.model,\n955\t    81\t                             \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason},\n956\t    82\t                )\n957\t    83\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n958\t    84\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n959\t    85\t                if not uses:\n960\t    86\t                    text = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n961\t    87\t                    items = _parse_items(text)\n962\t    88\t                    await audit.record(\n963\t    89\t                        self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"subagent_finished\", parent=start_node,\n964\t    90\t                        payload={\"items\": len(items)},\n965\t    91\t                    )\n966\t    92\t                    return items\n967\t    93\t                results = []\n968\t    94\t                for use in uses:\n969\t    95\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n970\t    96\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n971\t    97\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n972\t    98\t\n973\t    99\t        raise ExtractionFailed(f\"no result after {MAX_TURNS} turns\")\n974\t   100\t\n975\t   101\t\n976\t   102\tdef _parse_items(text: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n977\t   103\t    try:\n978\t   104\t        data = json.loads(text)\n979\t   105\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n980\t   106\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor returned non-JSON output\") from exc\n981\t   107\t    if not isinstance(data, list) or len(data) > 500:\n982\t   108\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor output must be a list of at most 500 items\")\n983\t   109\t    items = []\n984\t   110\t    for raw in data:\n985\t   111\t        if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not set(raw) <= LINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS:\n986\t   112\t            raise ExtractionFailed(\"unexpected line-item fields\")\n987\t   113\t        items.append({k: redact_for_model(v) if isinstance(v, str) else v for k, v in raw.items()})\n988\t   114\t    return items\n989\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d53973d-c6ec-47f2-bf1b-0f155eb7d218","uuid":"beeb9921-afa7-49bc-8430-f485fde5d963","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:12:33.583Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/brenn/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-6v-yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn-T-brace-batch-hh-5ij5h/7d53973d-c6ec-47f2-bf1b-0f155eb7d218/tool-results/bn5uugv8b.txt","content":"=== README.md\n     1\t# procurement-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tProcurement agent for Example Corp business units. It reads vendor quotes and\n     4\tinvoices that arrive by email, checks them against department budgets, raises\n     5\tpurchase orders in the ERP, pays matched invoices, and talks to staff and\n     6\tvendors in Slack. It keeps short per-department notes between runs.\n     7\t\n     8\t## Architecture\n     9\t\n    10\t```\n    11\tmail gateway --HMAC--> /ingest/mail --> documents (Postgres, per business unit)\n    12\tstaff (OIDC JWT) ----> /runs --> ProcurementAgent loop (app/loop.py)\n    13\t                                   |-- PolicyGate (app/gate.py) + approvals (Slack buttons)\n    14\t                                   |-- Budget (app/budget.py)\n    15\t                                   |-- audit graph (app/audit.py -> audit_events)\n    16\t                                   |-- tools:\n    17\t                                   |     read_document, extract_line_items -> LineItemExtractor sub-agent\n    18\t                                   |     get_budget, erp_call, create_purchase_order -> ERP MCP via gateway\n    19\t                                   |     pay_invoice -> payments API\n    20\t                                   |     post_slack_message -> Slack (via slack-proxy)\n    21\t                                   |     memory_read, memory_write -> dept_notes\n    22\t```\n    23\t\n    24\t* **Tenancy.** Each run belongs to one business unit, taken from the `bu`\n    25\t  claim of the caller's verified OIDC token. Documents, notes, approvals and\n    26\t  quotas are keyed by business unit.\n    27\t* **Identity.** The agent runs as the `procurement-agent` service account.\n    28\t  Its projected token (10-minute lifetime) is exchanged at the internal STS\n    29\t  for audience-bound tokens for the ERP gateway, payments API and Slack\n    30\t  proxy. User tokens are never forwarded.\n    31\t* **Approvals.** `create_purchase_order`, `pay_invoice` and vendor messages\n    32\t  require an approval from a role listed in `config/policy.yaml`. Approval\n    33\t  requests are posted to `#approvals-<bu>` with the argument summary.\n    34\t* **Budgets.** Per-run step, time, token, cost, tool-rate and sub-agent\n    35\t  limits, plus per-user, per-business-unit and fleet quotas for daily spend\n    36\t  and run starts. See `config/policy.yaml`.\n    37\t* **Audit.** Every run step is a row in `audit_events` linked to its parent\n    38\t  step, with the six identity fields, policy version, approval id and\n    39\t  decision-time context size. The agent's database role can insert audit\n    40\t  rows but not update or delete them.\n    41\t\n    42\t## Context size\n    43\t\n    44\tLogged on every audit row as `context_tokens` and `context_method`:\n    45\t\n    46\t| method | meaning |\n    47\t|---|---|\n    48\t| `count_tokens_api` | exact request counted with the provider's token-count endpoint before the call (includes cached prefix) |\n    49\t| `usage_sum_estimate` | counting failed; `input_tokens + cache_read + cache_creation` from the response |\n    50\t| `unavailable` | neither available; `context_tokens` is NULL, never 0 |\n    51\t\n    52\t`context_compacted` is true when the harness dropped earlier turns before the\n    53\tcall (`app/loop.py:_compact`). Provider-side truncation is not visible.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Operating\n    56\t\n    57\t* **Halt.** Insert or update a row in `control_flags` (`scope = 'fleet'` or\n    58\t  `'tenant:<bu>'`, `halted = true`) as `procurement_ops`. New runs refuse to\n    59\t  start while a halt is set.\n    60\t* **Release.** Merges to `main` build, sign (keyless cosign), and attest the\n    61\t  image (SLSA provenance and CycloneDX SBOM). Kyverno rejects unsigned or\n    62\t  unattested images in `procurement-prod`.\n    63\t* **Network.** Default-deny egress with explicit rules for DNS, the egress\n    64\t  proxy, the Slack proxy, the database, the ERP gateway and the STS.\n    65\t\n    66\t## Tests\n    67\t\n    68\t```bash\n    69\tpip install -e '.[test]'\n    70\tpytest -q\n    71\t```\n=== app/ingest.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Inbound documents: vendor quotes and invoices from the mail gateway.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe mail gateway posts each received message to ``/ingest/mail`` signed with\n     4\tan HMAC over the timestamp and body. Accepted documents are stored per\n     5\tbusiness unit and are only ever shown to the model inside an\n     6\t``untrusted_document`` wrapper (tools/documents.py).\n     7\t\"\"\"\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport base64\n    11\timport email\n    12\timport email.policy\n    13\timport hashlib\n    14\timport hmac\n    15\timport io\n    16\timport re\n    17\timport time\n    18\timport uuid\n    19\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    20\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    21\t\n    22\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, Request\n    23\tfrom pypdf import PdfReader\n    24\t\n    25\trouter = APIRouter()\n    26\t\n    27\tMAX_BODY_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n    28\tMAX_TEXT_CHARS = 200_000\n    29\tMAX_SKEW_SECONDS = 300\n    30\tALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\", \"message/rfc822\"}\n    31\tSCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES = {\"application/pdf\", \"text/plain\"}\n    32\t\n    33\tINJECTION_PATTERNS = [\n    34\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n    35\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system|developer) (prompt|message)\\b\"),\n    36\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are (now )?(an?|the) \\w+ (agent|assistant)\\b\"),\n    37\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) (the )?(pay_invoice|erp_call|create_purchase_order|post_slack_message|memory_write)\\b\"),\n    38\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(update|change) (our|the) (bank|remit|payee)\\b\"),\n    39\t    re.compile(r\"[​-‏‪-‮⁠-⁤]\"),\n    40\t]\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tclass Rejected(Exception):\n    44\t    pass\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t@dataclass\n    48\tclass Inbound:\n    49\t    business_unit: str\n    50\t    sender: str\n    51\t    media_type: str\n    52\t    raw: bytes\n    53\t\n    54\t\n    55\tdef verify_signature(key: bytes, timestamp: str, body: bytes, signature: str) -> None:\n    56\t    try:\n    57\t        ts = int(timestamp)\n    58\t    except ValueError as exc:\n    59\t        raise Rejected(\"bad timestamp\") from exc\n    60\t    if abs(time.time() - ts) > MAX_SKEW_SECONDS:\n    61\t        raise Rejected(\"stale request\")\n    62\t    expected = hmac.new(key, f\"{timestamp}.\".encode() + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    63\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(expected, signature):\n    64\t        raise Rejected(\"bad signature\")\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef extract_text(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    68\t    if doc.media_type == \"application/pdf\":\n    69\t        reader = PdfReader(io.BytesIO(doc.raw))\n    70\t        if len(reader.pages) > 50:\n    71\t            raise Rejected(\"too many pages\")\n    72\t        return \"\\n\".join(page.extract_text() or \"\" for page in reader.pages)\n    73\t    if doc.media_type == \"message/rfc822\":\n    74\t        msg = email.message_from_bytes(doc.raw, policy=email.policy.default)\n    75\t        body = msg.get_body(preferencelist=(\"plain\", \"html\"))\n    76\t        return body.get_content() if body is not None else \"\"\n    77\t    return doc.raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef scan_for_injection(text: str) -> list[str]:\n    81\t    return [p.pattern for p in INJECTION_PATTERNS if p.search(text)]\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\tdef validate(doc: Inbound) -> str:\n    85\t    if doc.media_type not in ALLOWED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    86\t        raise Rejected(f\"media type {doc.media_type} not accepted\")\n    87\t    if len(doc.raw) > MAX_BODY_BYTES:\n    88\t        raise Rejected(\"document too large\")\n    89\t    try:\n    90\t        text = extract_text(doc)\n    91\t    except Rejected:\n    92\t        raise\n    93\t    except Exception as exc:\n    94\t        raise Rejected(f\"unreadable document: {type(exc).__name__}\") from exc\n    95\t    if len(text) > MAX_TEXT_CHARS:\n    96\t        raise Rejected(\"extracted text too long\")\n    97\t    if doc.media_type in SCANNED_MEDIA_TYPES:\n    98\t        findings = scan_for_injection(text)\n    99\t        if findings:\n   100\t            raise Rejected(\"possible prompt injection: \" + \"; \".join(findings))\n   101\t    return text\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t@router.post(\"/ingest/mail\")\n   105\tasync def ingest_mail(request: Request) -> dict:\n   106\t    body = await request.body()\n   107\t    if len(body) > MAX_BODY_BYTES * 2:\n   108\t        raise HTTPException(413, \"payload too large\")\n   109\t    key = Path(request.app.state.settings.mail_gateway_hmac_path).read_bytes().strip()\n   110\t    try:\n   111\t        verify_signature(\n   112\t            key,\n   113\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Timestamp\", \"\"),\n   114\t            body,\n   115\t            request.headers.get(\"X-Gateway-Signature\", \"\"),\n   116\t        )\n   117\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   118\t        raise HTTPException(401, str(exc)) from exc\n   119\t\n   120\t    payload = await request.json()\n   121\t    doc = Inbound(\n   122\t        business_unit=payload[\"business_unit\"],\n   123\t        sender=payload[\"from\"],\n   124\t        media_type=payload[\"media_type\"],\n   125\t        raw=base64.b64decode(payload[\"content_b64\"], validate=True),\n   126\t    )\n   127\t    doc_id = f\"doc-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:20]}\"\n   128\t    pool = request.app.state.pool\n   129\t    try:\n   130\t        text = validate(doc)\n   131\t    except Rejected as exc:\n   132\t        await pool.execute(\n   133\t            \"\"\"\n   134\t            INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, reject_reason, received_at)\n   135\t            VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'quarantined', $6, now())\n   136\t            \"\"\",\n   137\t            doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   138\t            hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), str(exc)[:500],\n   139\t        )\n   140\t        return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"quarantined\"}\n   141\t\n   142\t    await pool.execute(\n   143\t        \"\"\"\n   144\t        INSERT INTO documents (doc_id, business_unit, source, media_type, sha256, status, text, received_at)\n   145\t        VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, 'accepted', $6, now())\n   146\t        \"\"\",\n   147\t        doc_id, doc.business_unit, doc.sender, doc.media_type,\n   148\t        hashlib.sha256(doc.raw).hexdigest(), text,\n   149\t    )\n   150\t    return {\"doc_id\": doc_id, \"status\": \"accepted\"}\n=== app/tools/memory.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Per-department notes kept between runs (Postgres ``dept_notes``).\n     2\t\n     3\tWrites are restricted to a fixed set of note kinds, length-limited, checked\n     4\tfor instruction-like content, and stored as unverified with a 30-day expiry\n     5\tuntil a procurement lead verifies them in the admin UI. Every row records\n     6\twho wrote it, from which run and source document, and the context size at\n     7\tthe time.\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    10\t\n    11\timport re\n    12\timport uuid\n    13\tfrom typing import Any\n    14\t\n    15\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    16\tfrom app.tools import Tool\n    17\t\n    18\tNOTE_KINDS = (\"vendor_preference\", \"contract_term\", \"budget_note\", \"contact\")\n    19\tMAX_NOTE_CHARS = 800\n    20\tINSTRUCTION_LIKE = [\n    21\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(ignore|disregard|override)\\b.{0,40}\\b(instruction|policy|approval|rule)s?\\b\"),\n    22\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(always|never|must)\\b.{0,40}\\b(approve|pay|skip|send|transfer)\\b\"),\n    23\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(system prompt|you are|assistant:)\\b\"),\n    24\t    re.compile(r\"https?://\"),\n    25\t]\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tclass NoteRejected(Exception):\n    29\t    pass\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tdef check_note(text: str) -> None:\n    33\t    if len(text) > MAX_NOTE_CHARS:\n    34\t        raise NoteRejected(\"note too long\")\n    35\t    for pattern in INSTRUCTION_LIKE:\n    36\t        if pattern.search(text):\n    37\t            raise NoteRejected(\"note looks like an instruction\")\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\tdef tools(deps) -> list[Tool]:\n    41\t    pool = deps.pool\n    42\t\n    43\t    async def memory_read(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n    44\t        business_unit = args.get(\"business_unit\") or ident.tenant\n    45\t        rows = await pool.fetch(\n    46\t            \"\"\"\n    47\t            SELECT note_id, kind, body, verified, writer_instance, created_at\n    48\t            FROM dept_notes\n    49\t            WHERE business_unit = $1\n    50\t              AND department = $2\n    51\t              AND NOT quarantined\n    52\t              AND (verified OR expires_at > now())\n    53\t            ORDER BY created_at DESC\n    54\t            LIMIT 20\n    55\t            \"\"\",\n    56\t            business_unit,\n    57\t            args[\"department\"],\n    58\t        )\n    59\t        return [\n    60\t            {\n    61\t                \"note_id\": r[\"note_id\"],\n    62\t                \"kind\": r[\"kind\"],\n    63\t                \"body\": r[\"body\"],\n    64\t                \"trust\": \"verified\" if r[\"verified\"] else \"unverified\",\n    65\t                \"written\": r[\"created_at\"].isoformat(),\n    66\t            }\n    67\t            for r in rows\n    68\t        ]\n    69\t\n    70\t    async def memory_write(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n    71\t        if args[\"kind\"] not in NOTE_KINDS:\n    72\t            raise NoteRejected(f\"unknown note kind {args['kind']}\")\n    73\t        check_note(args[\"body\"])\n    74\t        note_id = f\"note-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n    75\t        ctx = deps.current_context(ident)\n    76\t        await pool.execute(\n    77\t            \"\"\"\n    78\t            INSERT INTO dept_notes (\n    79\t                note_id, business_unit, department, kind, body,\n    80\t                verified, quarantined, expires_at,\n    81\t                writer_instance, writer_type_id, run_id, source_doc_id,\n    82\t                delegated_subject, context_tokens, context_method, created_at\n    83\t            ) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5, false, false, now() + interval '30 days',\n    84\t                      $6, $7, $8, $9, $10, $11, $12, now())\n    85\t            \"\"\",\n    86\t            note_id,\n    87\t            ident.tenant,\n    88\t            args[\"department\"],\n    89\t            args[\"kind\"],\n    90\t            args[\"body\"],\n    91\t            ident.agent_instance_id,\n    92\t            ident.agent_type_id,\n    93\t            ident.run_id,\n    94\t            args.get(\"source_doc_id\"),\n    95\t            ident.delegated_subject,\n    96\t            ctx.tokens,\n    97\t            ctx.method,\n    98\t        )\n    99\t        return {\"note_id\": note_id, \"status\": \"stored_unverified\"}\n   100\t\n   101\t    return [\n   102\t        Tool(\n   103\t            name=\"memory_read\",\n   104\t            description=(\n   105\t                \"Read saved notes for a department. business_unit defaults to the current one; \"\n   106\t                \"shared-services staff may look up another unit's notes.\"\n   107\t            ),\n   108\t            input_schema={\n   109\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n   110\t                \"properties\": {\n   111\t                    \"department\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n   112\t                    \"business_unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 32},\n   113\t                },\n   114\t                \"required\": [\"department\"],\n   115\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   116\t            },\n   117\t            invoke=memory_read,\n   118\t        ),\n   119\t        Tool(\n   120\t            name=\"memory_write\",\n   121\t            description=\"Save a short factual note for a department (vendor preference, contract term, budget note, contact).\",\n   122\t            input_schema={\n   123\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n   124\t                \"properties\": {\n   125\t                    \"department\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n   126\t                    \"kind\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": list(NOTE_KINDS)},\n   127\t                    \"body\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": MAX_NOTE_CHARS},\n   128\t                    \"source_doc_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64},\n   129\t                },\n   130\t                \"required\": [\"department\", \"kind\", \"body\"],\n   131\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n   132\t            },\n   133\t            invoke=memory_write,\n   134\t        ),\n   135\t    ]\n=== app/tools/documents.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Document tools: read an ingested quote or invoice, and extract line items.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\tfrom typing import Any\n     5\t\n     6\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n     7\tfrom app.tools import Tool\n     8\t\n     9\tUNTRUSTED_WRAPPER = (\n    10\t    \"<untrusted_document source={source!r} doc_id={doc_id!r} media_type={media_type!r}>\\n\"\n    11\t    \"{text}\\n\"\n    12\t    \"</untrusted_document>\"\n    13\t)\n    14\t\n    15\t\n    16\tdef tools(deps) -> list[Tool]:\n    17\t    pool = deps.pool\n    18\t\n    19\t    async def read_document(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> str:\n    20\t        row = await pool.fetchrow(\n    21\t            \"\"\"\n    22\t            SELECT doc_id, source, media_type, text\n    23\t            FROM documents\n    24\t            WHERE doc_id = $1 AND business_unit = $2 AND status = 'accepted'\n    25\t            \"\"\",\n    26\t            args[\"doc_id\"],\n    27\t            ident.tenant,\n    28\t        )\n    29\t        if row is None:\n    30\t            return \"document not found\"\n    31\t        return UNTRUSTED_WRAPPER.format(\n    32\t            source=row[\"source\"], doc_id=row[\"doc_id\"], media_type=row[\"media_type\"], text=row[\"text\"]\n    33\t        )\n    34\t\n    35\t    async def extract_line_items(args: dict[str, Any], ident: RunIdentity) -> Any:\n    36\t        return await deps.extractor.extract(ident, args[\"doc_id\"], deps.current_budget(ident))\n    37\t\n    38\t    return [\n    39\t        Tool(\n    40\t            name=\"read_document\",\n    41\t            description=\"Read the text of an ingested vendor quote, invoice, or email by doc_id.\",\n    42\t            input_schema={\n    43\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n    44\t                \"properties\": {\"doc_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64}},\n    45\t                \"required\": [\"doc_id\"],\n    46\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    47\t            },\n    48\t            invoke=read_document,\n    49\t        ),\n    50\t        Tool(\n    51\t            name=\"extract_line_items\",\n    52\t            description=\"Extract structured line items (sku, description, qty, unit price, currency) from a document.\",\n    53\t            input_schema={\n    54\t                \"type\": \"object\",\n    55\t                \"properties\": {\"doc_id\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"maxLength\": 64}},\n    56\t                \"required\": [\"doc_id\"],\n    57\t                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    58\t            },\n    59\t            invoke=extract_line_items,\n    60\t        ),\n    61\t    ]\n=== app/tools/__init__.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Tool registry.\n     2\t\n     3\tEach agent role gets the tools listed for it in config/tools.yaml. The model\n     4\tonly sees schemas for those tools, and the loop rejects any call to a name\n     5\tthat is not in the run's registry.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    10\tfrom functools import lru_cache\n    11\tfrom typing import Any, Awaitable, Callable\n    12\t\n    13\timport yaml\n    14\t\n    15\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    16\t\n    17\tDEFAULT_ROLE = \"procurement\"\n    18\t\n    19\tInvoke = Callable[[dict[str, Any], RunIdentity], Awaitable[Any]]\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    23\tclass Tool:\n    24\t    name: str\n    25\t    description: str\n    26\t    input_schema: dict[str, Any]\n    27\t    invoke: Invoke\n    28\t    target_field: str | None = None\n    29\t\n    30\t    def target_of(self, args: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    31\t        if self.target_field is None:\n    32\t            return self.name\n    33\t        return str(args.get(self.target_field, \"\"))\n    34\t\n    35\t    def schema(self) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    36\t        return {\"name\": self.name, \"description\": self.description, \"input_schema\": self.input_schema}\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tclass ToolRegistry:\n    40\t    def __init__(self, tools: list[Tool]):\n    41\t        self._tools = {t.name: t for t in tools}\n    42\t\n    43\t    def get(self, name: str) -> Tool | None:\n    44\t        return self._tools.get(name)\n    45\t\n    46\t    def names(self) -> list[str]:\n    47\t        return sorted(self._tools)\n    48\t\n    49\t    def schemas(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    50\t        return [self._tools[n].schema() for n in self.names()]\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\t@lru_cache(maxsize=1)\n    54\tdef _role_tools(path: str) -> dict[str, list[str]]:\n    55\t    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n    56\t        cfg = yaml.safe_load(fh)\n    57\t    return {role: list(spec[\"tools\"].keys()) for role, spec in cfg[\"roles\"].items()}\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef build_registry(role: str, ident: RunIdentity, deps) -> ToolRegistry:\n    61\t    from app.tools import documents, erp, memory, payments, slack\n    62\t\n    63\t    available: dict[str, Tool] = {}\n    64\t    for module in (documents, erp, memory, payments, slack):\n    65\t        for tool in module.tools(deps):\n    66\t            available[tool.name] = tool\n    67\t\n    68\t    roles = _role_tools(str(deps.settings.tools_path))\n    69\t    allowed = roles.get(role, roles[DEFAULT_ROLE])\n    70\t    return ToolRegistry([available[name] for name in allowed if name in available])\n=== app/context_size.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Decision-time context size.\n     2\t\n     3\tCounting method (documented in README, \"Context size\"):\n     4\t\n     5\t1. Before each model call, the exact request (system prompt, messages and\n     6\t   tool schemas) is sent to the provider's token-counting endpoint. The\n     7\t   returned ``input_tokens`` is recorded with method ``count_tokens_api``.\n     8\t   This is the size of the context the model decides on, including any\n     9\t   prefix that will be served from the prompt cache.\n    10\t2. If counting fails, the value is taken after the call from the response\n    11\t   usage as ``input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens +\n    12\t   cache_creation_input_tokens`` and recorded with method\n    13\t   ``usage_sum_estimate``.\n    14\t3. If neither is available the value is ``NULL`` with method\n    15\t   ``unavailable``. It is never recorded as zero.\n    16\t\n    17\t``compacted`` is true when the harness dropped or summarized earlier turns\n    18\tbefore this call. Provider-side truncation is not visible to the harness and\n    19\tis listed as a known limit.\n    20\t\"\"\"\n    21\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    22\t\n    23\timport logging\n    24\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, replace\n    25\t\n    26\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n    30\tclass ContextMeasure:\n    31\t    tokens: int | None\n    32\t    method: str\n    33\t    compacted: bool\n    34\t\n    35\t    @classmethod\n    36\t    def unavailable(cls, compacted: bool = False) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    37\t        return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\n    38\t\n    39\t    def finalize(self, usage) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n    40\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    41\t            return self\n    42\t        if usage is None:\n    43\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    44\t        total = (\n    45\t            int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n    46\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    47\t            + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n    48\t        )\n    49\t        if total <= 0:\n    50\t            return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n    51\t        return replace(self, tokens=total, method=\"usage_sum_estimate\")\n    52\t\n    53\t    def otel_attributes(self) -> dict:\n    54\t        attrs = {\n    55\t            \"procurement.context.method\": self.method,\n    56\t            \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": self.compacted,\n    57\t        }\n    58\t        if self.tokens is not None:\n    59\t            attrs[\"procurement.context.tokens\"] = self.tokens\n    60\t        return attrs\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tasync def measure_context(client, request: dict, compacted: bool) -> ContextMeasure:\n    64\t    try:\n    65\t        counted = await client.messages.count_tokens(\n    66\t            model=request[\"model\"],\n    67\t            system=request[\"system\"],\n    68\t            messages=request[\"messages\"],\n    69\t            tools=request[\"tools\"],\n    70\t        )\n    71\t        return ContextMeasure(int(counted.input_tokens), \"count_tokens_api\", compacted)\n    72\t    except Exception:  # counting is best effort; finalize() falls back to usage\n    73\t        log.warning(\"token count failed; falling back to usage\", exc_info=True)\n    74\t        return ContextMeasure(tokens=None, method=\"pending_usage\", compacted=compacted)\n=== app/audit.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Execution audit graph.\n     2\t\n     3\tEvery step of a run is one row in ``audit_events``. Rows link to their parent\n     4\tstep, so a run can be rebuilt as a tree: run -> model decision -> proposed\n     5\ttool call -> authorization decision -> result or error. Writes are\n     6\tsynchronous and are made before the action they describe; if the write\n     7\tfails, the caller raises and the action does not run.\n     8\t\"\"\"\n     9\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    10\t\n    11\timport hashlib\n    12\timport json\n    13\timport uuid\n    14\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n    15\tfrom typing import Any\n    16\t\n    17\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    18\t\n    19\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure\n    20\tfrom app.identity import IDENTITY_FIELDS, RunIdentity\n    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_value\n    22\t\n    23\tEVENT_KINDS = {\n    24\t    \"run_started\",\n    25\t    \"run_finished\",\n    26\t    \"run_halted\",\n    27\t    \"model_decision\",\n    28\t    \"tool_proposed\",\n    29\t    \"authz_decision\",\n    30\t    \"approval_requested\",\n    31\t    \"approval_decided\",\n    32\t    \"tool_result\",\n    33\t    \"tool_error\",\n    34\t    \"tool_denied\",\n    35\t    \"budget_exceeded\",\n    36\t    \"subagent_started\",\n    37\t    \"subagent_finished\",\n    38\t    \"background_job\",\n    39\t}\n    40\t\n    41\t_INSERT = \"\"\"\n    42\tINSERT INTO audit_events (\n    43\t    node_id, parent_node_id, run_id, ts, kind,\n    44\t    accountable_party, operational_owner, tenant,\n    45\t    agent_type_id, agent_instance_id, trace_id, span_id,\n    46\t    delegated_subject, agent_principal, parent_instance_id,\n    47\t    policy_version, approval_id, operation_id,\n    48\t    context_tokens, context_method, context_compacted,\n    49\t    payload\n    50\t) VALUES (\n    51\t    $1, $2, $3, $4, $5,\n    52\t    $6, $7, $8,\n    53\t    $9, $10, $11, $12,\n    54\t    $13, $14, $15,\n    55\t    $16, $17, $18,\n    56\t    $19, $20, $21,\n    57\t    $22::jsonb\n    58\t)\n    59\t\"\"\"\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\tdef summarize_args(args: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    63\t    \"\"\"Key arguments for the record, with secrets and account numbers redacted.\"\"\"\n    64\t    return {k: redact_value(v) for k, v in args.items()}\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\tdef digest(value: Any) -> str:\n    68\t    raw = json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, default=str, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n    69\t    return hashlib.sha256(raw.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\tasync def record(\n    73\t    pool,\n    74\t    ident: RunIdentity,\n    75\t    *,\n    76\t    kind: str,\n    77\t    payload: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    78\t    parent: str | None = None,\n    79\t    context: ContextMeasure | None = None,\n    80\t    policy_version: str | None = None,\n    81\t    approval_id: str | None = None,\n    82\t    operation_id: str | None = None,\n    83\t) -> str:\n    84\t    if kind not in EVENT_KINDS:\n    85\t        raise ValueError(f\"unknown audit kind {kind}\")\n    86\t    for name in IDENTITY_FIELDS:\n    87\t        if not getattr(ident, name):\n    88\t            raise ValueError(f\"audit record missing {name}\")\n    89\t    span_ctx = trace.get_current_span().get_span_context()\n    90\t    span_id = format(span_ctx.span_id, \"016x\") if span_ctx.is_valid else None\n    91\t    node_id = f\"node-{uuid.uuid4()}\"\n    92\t    measure = context or ContextMeasure.unavailable()\n    93\t    await pool.execute(\n    94\t        _INSERT,\n    95\t        node_id,\n    96\t        parent,\n    97\t        ident.run_id,\n    98\t        datetime.now(timezone.utc),\n    99\t        kind,\n   100\t        ident.accountable_party,\n   101\t        ident.operational_owner,\n   102\t        ident.tenant,\n   103\t        ident.agent_type_id,\n   104\t        ident.agent_instance_id,\n   105\t        ident.trace_id,\n   106\t        span_id,\n   107\t        ident.delegated_subject,\n   108\t        ident.agent_principal,\n   109\t        ident.parent_instance_id,\n   110\t        policy_version,\n   111\t        approval_id,\n   112\t        operation_id,\n   113\t        measure.tokens,\n   114\t        measure.method,\n   115\t        measure.compacted,\n   116\t        json.dumps(redact_value(payload or {}), default=str),\n   117\t    )\n   118\t    return node_id\n=== app/loop.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Procurement agent run loop.\n     2\t\n     3\tGraph: model turn -> (tool calls -> gate -> integration)* -> model turn ...\n     4\tEvery edge writes an audit node before the next step runs. Budgets are\n     5\tchecked before each model turn and each tool call.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\timport hashlib\n    10\timport logging\n    11\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n    12\tfrom typing import Any\n    13\t\n    14\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    15\t\n    16\tfrom app import audit, killswitch\n    17\tfrom app.budget import Budget, BudgetExceeded\n    18\tfrom app.context_size import ContextMeasure, measure_context\n    19\tfrom app.gate import PolicyGate\n    20\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    21\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n    22\tfrom app.tools import ToolRegistry, build_registry\n    23\t\n    24\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    25\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.loop\")\n    26\t\n    27\tCOMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES = 40\n    28\tKEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES = 12\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t@dataclass\n    32\tclass AgentDeps:\n    33\t    settings: Any\n    34\t    pool: Any\n    35\t    gate: PolicyGate\n    36\t    erp: Any\n    37\t    slack: Any\n    38\t    broker: Any\n    39\t    extractor: Any = None\n    40\t    _budgets: dict[str, Budget] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    41\t    _contexts: dict[str, ContextMeasure] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    42\t\n    43\t    def current_budget(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> Budget:\n    44\t        return self._budgets[ident.run_id]\n    45\t\n    46\t    def current_context(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> ContextMeasure:\n    47\t        return self._contexts.get(ident.agent_instance_id, ContextMeasure.unavailable())\n    48\t\n    49\t    def erp_scope_for(self, operation: str) -> str:\n    50\t        scopes = self.settings.policy[\"erp\"][\"operation_scopes\"]\n    51\t        return scopes.get(operation, \"erp.read\")\n    52\t\n    53\t    async def execute_tool(self, ident, registry: ToolRegistry, use, parent: str, ctx: ContextMeasure) -> dict:\n    54\t        self._contexts[ident.agent_instance_id] = ctx\n    55\t        proposed = await audit.record(\n    56\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_proposed\", parent=parent, context=ctx,\n    57\t            payload={\"tool\": use.name, \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"args\": audit.summarize_args(use.input)},\n    58\t        )\n    59\t        tool = registry.get(use.name)\n    60\t        if tool is None:\n    61\t            await audit.record(\n    62\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_denied\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n    63\t                policy_version=self.gate.version, payload={\"reason\": \"tool not in role allowlist\"},\n    64\t            )\n    65\t            return _error(use.id, f\"tool {use.name} is not available to this agent\")\n    66\t\n    67\t        decision = await self.gate.authorize(ident, tool, use.input)\n    68\t        authz = await audit.record(\n    69\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"authz_decision\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n    70\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n    71\t            payload={\"allow\": decision.allow, \"reason\": decision.reason, \"pending\": decision.pending},\n    72\t        )\n    73\t        if not decision.allow:\n    74\t            if decision.pending:\n    75\t                return _error(use.id, f\"approval requested ({decision.approval_id}); do not retry until approved\")\n    76\t            return _error(use.id, f\"denied: {decision.reason}\")\n    77\t\n    78\t        operation_id = f\"op-{hashlib.sha256((authz + use.id).encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}\"\n    79\t        try:\n    80\t            with tracer.start_as_current_span(f\"execute_tool {use.name}\") as span:\n    81\t                for k, v in ctx.otel_attributes().items():\n    82\t                    span.set_attribute(k, v)\n    83\t                output = await tool.invoke(use.input, ident)\n    84\t        except BudgetExceeded:\n    85\t            raise\n    86\t        except Exception as exc:\n    87\t            await audit.record(\n    88\t                self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_error\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n    89\t                policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n    90\t                operation_id=operation_id,\n    91\t                payload={\"error_type\": type(exc).__name__, \"error\": str(exc)[:500]},\n    92\t            )\n    93\t            return _error(use.id, f\"{use.name} failed: {type(exc).__name__}\")\n    94\t\n    95\t        await audit.record(\n    96\t            self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_result\", parent=authz, context=ctx,\n    97\t            policy_version=decision.policy_version, approval_id=decision.approval_id,\n    98\t            operation_id=operation_id,\n    99\t            payload={\"result_sha256\": audit.digest(output), \"result\": output},\n   100\t        )\n   101\t        return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"content\": redact_for_model(output)}\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\tdef _error(tool_use_id: str, message: str) -> dict:\n   105\t    return {\"type\": \"tool_result\", \"tool_use_id\": tool_use_id, \"is_error\": True, \"content\": message}\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef _compact(messages: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], bool]:\n   109\t    if len(messages) <= COMPACT_AFTER_MESSAGES:\n   110\t        return messages, False\n   111\t    head, tail = messages[:1], messages[-KEEP_RECENT_MESSAGES:]\n   112\t    while tail and tail[0][\"role\"] != \"assistant\":\n   113\t        tail = tail[1:]\n   114\t    note = {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[earlier tool exchanges were removed to save space]\"}\n   115\t    return head + [note] + tail, True\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\tclass ProcurementAgent:\n   119\t    def __init__(self, *, client, deps: AgentDeps, system_prompt: str, role: str = \"procurement\"):\n   120\t        self.client = client\n   121\t        self.deps = deps\n   122\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n   123\t        self.role = role\n   124\t\n   125\t    async def run(self, ident: RunIdentity, task: str) -> str | None:\n   126\t        pool = self.deps.pool\n   127\t        await killswitch.assert_running(pool, ident.tenant)\n   128\t        budget = Budget.for_run(self.deps.settings.budgets, ident)\n   129\t        await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n   130\t        self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n   131\t        registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n   132\t\n   133\t        run_node = await audit.record(\n   134\t            pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n   135\t            payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n   136\t        )\n   137\t        messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n   138\t        try:\n   139\t            while True:\n   140\t                budget.check_step()\n   141\t                messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\n   142\t                request = {\n   143\t                    \"model\": self.deps.settings.model_id,\n   144\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n   145\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n   146\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n   147\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n   148\t                }\n   149\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted)\n   150\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n   151\t                budget.charge_model(self.deps.settings.model_id, response.usage)\n   152\t                await budget.flush(pool)\n   153\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n   154\t                decision = await audit.record(\n   155\t                    pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n   156\t                    payload={\n   157\t                        \"requested_model\": request[\"model\"],\n   158\t                        \"served_model\": response.model,\n   159\t                        \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason,\n   160\t                        \"proposed_tools\": [b.name for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"],\n   161\t                    },\n   162\t                )\n   163\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n   164\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n   165\t                if not uses:\n   166\t                    final = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n   167\t                    await audit.record(pool, ident, kind=\"run_finished\", parent=run_node, context=ctx,\n   168\t                                       payload={\"final_sha256\": audit.digest(final)})\n   169\t                    return final\n   170\t                results = []\n   171\t                for use in uses:\n   172\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n   173\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n   174\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n   175\t        except BudgetExceeded as exc:\n   176\t            await audit.record(\n   177\t                pool, ident, kind=\"budget_exceeded\", parent=run_node,\n   178\t                payload={\"limit\": exc.limit, \"used\": str(exc.used), \"allowed\": str(exc.allowed)},\n   179\t            )\n   180\t            await self.deps.slack.post(\n   181\t                channel=\"#procurement-agent-ops\",\n   182\t                text=f\"Run {ident.run_id} ({ident.tenant}) stopped: {exc.limit} exceeded.\",\n   183\t            )\n   184\t            return None\n   185\t        finally:\n   186\t            self.deps._budgets.pop(ident.run_id, None)\n=== app/extractor.py\n     1\t\"\"\"Line-item extraction sub-agent.\n     2\t\n     3\tThe parent procurement agent delegates structured extraction to a smaller\n     4\tmodel. The child runs under its own instance id, links to its parent in the\n     5\taudit graph, charges the parent's budget, and gets the extractor tool role.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     8\t\n     9\timport json\n    10\timport logging\n    11\tfrom typing import Any\n    12\t\n    13\tfrom opentelemetry import trace\n    14\t\n    15\tfrom app import audit\n    16\tfrom app.budget import Budget\n    17\tfrom app.context_size import measure_context\n    18\tfrom app.identity import RunIdentity\n    19\tfrom app.redact import redact_for_model\n    20\tfrom app.tools import build_registry\n    21\t\n    22\tlog = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n    23\ttracer = trace.get_tracer(\"procurement.extractor\")\n    24\t\n    25\tEXTRACTOR_ROLE = \"line_item_extractor\"\n    26\tMAX_TURNS = 4\n    27\t\n    28\tLINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS = {\"sku\", \"description\", \"quantity\", \"unit_price_cents\", \"currency\"}\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tclass ExtractionFailed(Exception):\n    32\t    pass\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tclass LineItemExtractor:\n    36\t    def __init__(self, *, client, settings, deps, system_prompt: str):\n    37\t        self.client = client\n    38\t        self.settings = settings\n    39\t        self.deps = deps\n    40\t        self.system_prompt = system_prompt\n    41\t\n    42\t    async def extract(self, parent: RunIdentity, doc_id: str, budget: Budget) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    43\t        budget.check_subagent()\n    44\t        ident = parent.child(role=EXTRACTOR_ROLE)\n    45\t        registry = build_registry(EXTRACTOR_ROLE, ident, self.deps)\n    46\t        task = f\"Extract every line item from document {doc_id}. Return JSON only.\"\n    47\t\n    48\t        with tracer.start_as_current_span(\"gen_ai.invoke_agent line_item_extractor\") as span:\n    49\t            span.set_attribute(\"gen_ai.agent.id\", ident.agent_instance_id)\n    50\t            span.set_attribute(\"procurement.parent_instance_id\", parent.agent_instance_id)\n    51\t            start_node = await audit.record(\n    52\t                self.deps.pool,\n    53\t                ident,\n    54\t                kind=\"subagent_started\",\n    55\t                payload={\n    56\t                    \"role\": EXTRACTOR_ROLE,\n    57\t                    \"doc_id\": doc_id,\n    58\t                    \"parent_prompt_ref\": format(span.get_span_context().span_id, \"016x\"),\n    59\t                    \"tools\": registry.names(),\n    60\t                },\n    61\t            )\n    62\t\n    63\t            messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n    64\t            for _turn in range(MAX_TURNS):\n    65\t                budget.check_step()\n    66\t                request = {\n    67\t                    \"model\": self.settings.extractor_model_id,\n    68\t                    \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n    69\t                    \"messages\": messages,\n    70\t                    \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n    71\t                    \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n    72\t                }\n    73\t                ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted=False)\n    74\t                response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n    75\t                budget.charge_model(self.settings.extractor_model_id, response.usage)\n    76\t                await budget.flush(self.deps.pool)\n    77\t                ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n    78\t                decision = await audit.record(\n    79\t                    self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,\n    80\t                    payload={\"requested_model\": request[\"model\"], \"served_model\": response.model,\n    81\t                             \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason},\n    82\t                )\n    83\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n    84\t                uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n    85\t                if not uses:\n    86\t                    text = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n    87\t                    items = _parse_items(text)\n    88\t                    await audit.record(\n    89\t                        self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"subagent_finished\", parent=start_node,\n    90\t                        payload={\"items\": len(items)},\n    91\t                    )\n    92\t                    return items\n    93\t                results = []\n    94\t                for use in uses:\n    95\t                    budget.check_tool_call()\n    96\t                    results.append(await self.deps.execute_tool(ident, registry, use, decision, ctx))\n    97\t                messages.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": results})\n    98\t\n    99\t        raise ExtractionFailed(f\"no result after {MAX_TURNS} turns\")\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef _parse_items(text: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n   103\t    try:\n   104\t        data = json.loads(text)\n   105\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n   106\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor returned non-JSON output\") from exc\n   107\t    if not isinstance(data, list) or len(data) > 500:\n   108\t        raise ExtractionFailed(\"extractor output must be a list of at most 500 items\")\n   109\t    items = []\n   110\t    for raw in data:\n   111\t        if not isinstance(raw, dict) or not set(raw) <= LINE_ITEMS_SCHEMA_KEYS:\n   112\t            raise ExtractionFailed(\"unexpected line-item fields\")\n   113\t        items.append({k: redact_for_model(v) if isinstance(v, str) else v for k, v in raw.items()})\n   114\t    return items\n","numLines":989,"startLine":1,"totalLines":989}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WS4KJfzczxz1G6R165RJKx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
